  "abstract": "<p>\n                    For an integer\n                    <italic>n</italic>\n                    , let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(n)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    denote the smallest\n                    <italic>x</italic>\n                    such that the primes\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"less-than-or-equal-to x\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ≤\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\leq x</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    generate the multiplicative group modulo\n                    <italic>n</italic>\n                    . We offer heuristic arguments and numerical data supporting the idea that\n                    <disp-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      \\[\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis less-than-or-equal-to left-parenthesis log 2 right-parenthesis Superscript negative 1 Baseline log n log log n\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ≤\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ⁡\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                  <mml:mo>\n                                    −\n                                    \n                                  </mml:mo>\n                                  <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                                </mml:mrow>\n                              </mml:msup>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(n) \\leq {(\\log 2)^{ - 1}}\\log n\\log \\log n</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                      \\]\n                    </disp-formula>\n                    asymptotically. We believe that the coefficient\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1 slash log 2\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo>/</mml:mo>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1/\\log 2</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is optimal. Finally, we show the average value of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(n)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    for\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n less-than-or-equal-to upper N\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ≤\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n \\leq N</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is at least\n                    <disp-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      \\[\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left-parenthesis 1 plus o left-parenthesis 1 right-parenthesis right-parenthesis log log upper N log log log upper N comma\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>+</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>o</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⁡\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>N</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(1 + o(1))\\log \\log N\\log \\log \\log N,</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                      \\]\n                    </disp-formula>\n                    and give a heuristic argument that this is also an upper bound. This work gives additional evidence, independent of the ERH, that primality testing can be done in deterministic polynomial time; if our bound on\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper G left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>G</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">G(n)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    is correct, there is a deterministic primality test using\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper O left-parenthesis log n right-parenthesis squared\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>O</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>log</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                ⁡\n                                \n                              </mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mi>n</mml:mi>\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                              </mml:msup>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">O{(\\log n)^2}</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    multiplications modulo\n                    <italic>n</italic>\n                    .\n                  </p>",
